# UDP Port Scan

## Objective
Identify open UDP ports and services running on the target host (192.168.1.114) using nmap's UDP scan technique

## Command used
nmap -sU -v 192.168.1.114

-sU: Perfoms a UDP scan to identify open UDP services.

# How UDP scan works
Unlike TCP, UDP does not use a three-way handshake. Nmap sends UDP packets to target ports and analyses the responses.

Responses are interpreted as:
- Response receieved: Port is open
- ICMP Port is unreachable response: Port is closed
- No response: Port is open|filtered

