# Analysis
The UDP scan identified several UDP services that were not visible during TCP-only scanning.

Important discoveries include:
- UDP port 53
Indicates a DNS service is running

-UDP port 111
Indicates RPCBind is available, which is commonly associated with RPC services.

-UDP port 2049
Indicates NFS (Network File System), whihc may allow network file sharing.

-UDP port 137
Indicates NetBIOS name services

This scan took significantly longer than TCP scans because UDP does not establish a connection. Nmap must wait for responses or timeouts to determine the state of each port.

## Conclusion
The UDP scan revealed additional services on the target host that would not have been discovered through the TCP scanning alone. Performing both the TCP and UDP scans provides a more complete view of the target's attack surface.